HX710B Pressure Sensor with ESP32
1. Project Overview

This project demonstrates interfacing the HX710B pressure sensor module with an ESP32 microcontroller to acquire, process, and calibrate pressure-related sensor data.

This project is part of my Journey of Sensors in Biomedical repository, where I document my learning, experiments, source code, and practical implementations involving sensors and biomedical instrumentation.

2. Components Required
ESP32 Development Board

The main controller used to read sensor data, process measurements, and send results to the Serial Monitor or other connected applications.

HX710B Pressure Sensor Module

A high-resolution measurement module that converts the electrical signal from a compatible pressure transducer into digital data.

Pressure Transducer

Detects applied pressure and converts it into an electrical signal. The type and pressure range depend on the transducer used.

Jumper Wires

Used to connect the ESP32 and HX710B module.

USB Cable

Used to program and power the ESP32 and view serial output.

3. ESP32 Pin Connections

Example connections for a module with VCC, GND, DOUT, and SCK pins:

HX710B Module	ESP32 Board	Function
VCC	3V3, if supported	Power supply
GND	GND	Common ground
DOUT	GPIO 18	Digital data output
SCK	GPIO 19	Clock signal

Note: GPIO 18 and GPIO 19 are example assignments. Confirm the pin numbers used in the source code and the voltage requirements of your specific module before connecting the hardware.

