5. Working Principle
Pressure is applied to a compatible pressure transducer.
The transducer converts pressure into an electrical signal.
The HX710B measurement IC converts the signal into digital data.
The ESP32 reads the digital output using the appropriate communication protocol.
The program processes and displays or records the sensor readings.
Calibration can be used to convert raw readings into pressure units.
