7. Calibration and Testing

Calibration is necessary to relate raw sensor readings to known pressure values.

Recommended testing procedure:

Record readings under a known reference condition.
Apply multiple known pressure values within the transducer's rated range.
Record the corresponding raw sensor readings.
Calculate and verify the calibration relationship.
Document the calibration factor, pressure units, reference instrument, and measurement range.

Raw readings must not be treated as pressure values until the conversion has been verified.

